Subject: wasix: let a runtime replace module compilation

The first compilation of a spawned module happens lazily inside the
runtime, on a global Rayon pool that is created on first use and never
torn down. An embedder that stops every thread and forks, as a host
that freezes guests does, cannot tolerate permanent compiler workers
appearing as a side effect of an exec. Add a ModuleCompiler hook to
the Runtime trait: when it is set, a module cache miss compiles
through the callback, and the embedder chooses where that work runs,
for example a disposable pool it joins before returning. The test
checks the hook is used once and the cache answers from then on.

